  "_what": "Remote-admin v2 slice 0e-B extra-pins manifest (R-RA-2). Read by `tools/probe_board_abi.py --extra-pins tools/radmin_0e_abi_pins.json`. It pins the CANDIDATE value types declared in test/radmin_0e_candidate_types.h on host, ARM (gateway) and Xtensa (heltec_mobile). These are MEASUREMENTS, not decisions: no capacity, timer or production type is ruled by this file.",
  "_derivation": "Measured 2026-09-04 at HEAD ecef942 by the probe's own compile-and-read mechanism (generate_tu + measure) on each env's real `pio run -t idedata` toolchain and flag set. Every candidate is fixed-width and pointer-free, so all three ABIs agree; `radmin0e::AbiWitnessNotACandidate` is the deliberate control that DOES diverge (host 24/8 vs both boards 12/4), which is what proves the overlay can see an ABI difference.",
